Synthesis in the Primitive Ocean](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-94-009-8420-2_18)\n17. [Prebiotic synthesis of \u03b1-amino acids and orotate from \u03b1-ketoacids potentiates transition to extant metabolic pathways](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41557-022-00999-w)\n18. [Biomolecules from HCN](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-94-010-2239-2_12)\n19. [hydantoins: Topics by Science.gov](https://www.science.gov/topicpages/h/hydantoins.html)\n20. [HCN: A plausible source of purines, pyrimidines and amino acids on the primitive earth](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01733839)\n21. [Chemical evolution](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01797455)\n22. [Simple Organics and Biomonomers Identified in HCN Polymers: An Overview](https://doi.org/10.3390/life3030421)\n23. [Structural studies on HCN oligomers](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01732676)\n24. [Common origins of RNA, protein and lipid precursors in a cyanosulfidic protometabolism.](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Common-origins-of-RNA,-protein-and-lipid-precursors-Patel-Percivalle/3b482858daca31713acd680830b446c96e0ee8d5)\n25. [Prebiotic Reaction Networks in Water - PMC - NIH](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7765580/)\n26. [Cyanosulfidic prebiotic synthesis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyanosulfidic_prebiotic_synthesis)\n27. [Common origins of RNA, protein and lipid precursors in a cyanosulfidic protometabolism](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/274088015_Common_origins_of_RNA_protein_and_lipid_precursors_in_a_cyanosulfidic_protometabolism)\n28. [Quantifying Reductive Amination in Nonenzymatic Amino Acid Synthesis](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9828492/)\n29. [Synthesis and breakdown of universal metabolic precursors promoted by iron](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-019-1151-1)\n30. [Synthesis and breakdown of universal metabolic precursors promoted by iron - PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6517