ence branch, without invoking molecular oxygen. Numeric conditions identified as screening windows are proposed tests, not reported kinetic measurements. Shared molecular IDs denote chemical identity, not compulsory mixing: cyanide/copper/sulfide chemistry and metal-catalyzed glyoxylate chemistry occupy separate habitats. Transfers and changes of pH within a pathway are specified below. The single environment_formed value records a representative formation setting; null denotes a supplied boundary species. The schema's intermediate role also covers non-target coproducts. Product formation does not automatically establish dissolved availability, particularly on brucite.\n\nMOLECULES (25 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2O (Water) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CH4 (Methane) [starting]\n  - mol_003: NH3 (Ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CHN (Hydrogen cyanide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: CH2O (Formaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_006: H2 (Molecular hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_007: CH3N (Formaldimine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C2H4N2 (Aminoacetonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C2H6N2O (Glycinamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C2H5NO2 (Glycine) [target]\n  - mol_011: C2H3NO (Glycolonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C2H4O3 (Glycolic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C2H2O3 (Glyoxylic acid) [starting]\n  - mol_014: C2H3NO2 (Glycine imine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_015: H2S (Hydrogen sulfide) [starting]\n  - mol_016: S8 (Elemental sulfur) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: Fe+2 (Ferrous ion) [starting]\n  - mol_018: H+ (Proton equivalent) [starting]\n  - mol_019: FeH2O2 (Ferrous hydroxide redox endmember) [starting]\n  - mol_020: FeHO2 (Ferric oxyhydroxide redox endmember) [starting]\n  - mol_021: H3NO (Hydroxylamine) [starting]\n  - mol_022: C2H3NO3 (Glyoxylic acid oxime) [intermediate]\n  - mol_023: Fe (Native iron) [starting]\n  - mol_024: NO3- (Nitrate ion) [starting]\n  - mol_025: C4H7NO4 (Iminodiacetic acid) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (22 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_002, mol_003, mol_001 -> mol_004, mol_005, mol_006 (Reducing-atmosphere discharge production of Strecker feedstocks) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_004, mol_015, mol_001 -> mol_005, mol_003, mol_016 (Sulfide-driven photoreduction of HCN to a formaldehyde precursor pool) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_007, mol_001 (Reversible formaldehyde-ammonia condensation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_007, mol_004 -> mol_008 (Cyanide capture of methanimine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_005, mol_004 -> mol_011 (Formaldehyde cyanohydrin formation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_011, mol_003 -> mol_008, mol_001 (Ammonia-driven conversion of glycolonitrile to aminoacetonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_008, mol_001 -> mol_009 (Aminoacetonitrile hydration to glycinamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_009, mol_001 -> mol_010, mol_003 (Glycinamide hydrolysis and glycine release) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_005, mol_003, mol_004 -> mol_008, mol_001 (Hydrothermal Strecker aminonitrile formation) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_010: mol_008, mol_001 -> mol_010, mol_003 (Hydrothermal aminonitrile hydrolysis to glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_011, mol_001 -> mol_012, mol_003 (Competing glycolonitrile hydrolysis to glycolate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_013, mol_003 -> mol_014, mol_001 (Reversible glyoxylate-ammonia condensation to glycine imine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_013: mol_014, mol_017, mol_001 -> mol_010, mol_020, mol_018 (Dissolved Fe(II)-mediated imine reduction with ferric hydrolysis) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_014: mol_014, mol_019, mol_020 -> mol_010, mol_020 (Mixed-valence iron-hydroxide surface reduction of glycine imine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_015: mol_014, mol_019 -> mol_010, mol_020 (Ferroan-brucite reduction of ammonia-derived glycine imine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_016: mol_013, mol_024, mol_018, mol_019 -> mol_010, mol_020, mol_001 (Coupled nitrate reduction and glyoxylate amination on ferroan brucite) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_017: mol_014, mol_006 -> mol_0